  "steps": [
    "Marinate the chicken: Pat the thighs dry and season both sides with 1 tsp salt and 1/2 tsp pepper. Whisk the harissa, garlic, lemon zest, lemon juice, and honey in a large bowl. Add the chicken and toss to coat. Cover and refrigerate at least 30 minutes, or up to a day.",
    "Cook the rice while the chicken marinates: Bring the water or stock, olive oil, and 1 tsp salt to a boil in a medium saucepan. Add the rice, return to a boil, then cover, reduce the heat to low, and simmer 30 minutes without lifting the lid. If liquid remains, simmer in 5-minute increments until absorbed.",
    "Turn off the heat and let the rice rest, covered, for 10 minutes. Fluff with a fork and season with 1/2 tsp pepper and the parsley.",
    "Preheat the oven to 400°F with a rack in the center. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper.",
    "Bake the chicken: Arrange the thighs on the sheet and brush with any leftover marinade. Bake 13-15 minutes, until the thickest part reads 165°F.",
    "Rest the chicken under foil for 10 minutes, then cut into bite-sized cubes.",
    "Make the vinaigrette: Combine all the vinaigrette ingredients in a mason jar, cover, and shake until emulsified, about 30 seconds. Adjust the seasoning to taste.",
    "Assemble: Divide the rice among 6 bowls and top with the greens, chicken, cucumber, tomatoes, pickled onions, olives, and corn. Add a dollop each of hummus, tzatziki, and feta. Drizzle with the vinaigrette and serve with pita chips if you like."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "The Foolproof Living card uses 1/4 cup honey in the marinade and 1/4 cup oil in the vinaigrette; this version runs a little sweeter and richer with 1/3 cup of each."
  ],
